                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've come to appreciate the following equation...\n\nGame Guru = Can't Code\n\nHiking simulator is a blatant cash grab from an affiliation of shonky marketers. That being said, the most surprising thing is that the ring leader behind it all, is Rasmus Ladegaard the developer and producer behind the tv docu series 'The history of Video games' http://www.imdb.com/title/tt6178594/?ref_=nm_flmg_wr_4\n\n6 walking tracks that require you to walk around in a circle where several npc animals have been placed and are programmed to run away if you ever get close. Talking about the animals, why do they all walk like they have something stuck up their butt? Why are there trees floating in the air? Why does water kill you if you touch it? Why can't I pick anything up? Why did I buy this??? \n\nYes, there is nothing to do in this game other than walk, jump, and be a lemming at the top of a cliff. It is possible to climb the boundaries if you are persistent enough to find the glitches and you then can go see what the edge of the map looks like and the Easter egg of the words 'Moo' at the farm.\n\nThe only positive was the 6 superlative accompanying music tracks, but alas they too are temperamental in the game cutting in and out as they feel like it. If you want to actually listen to them you really need to locate the folder they are in and play them direct.\n\nIn final, a poor graphical piled together asset heap, with no serious forethought or effort placed in it to give customers value for money. Yes take the game's advice ... 'Walk Away!!!'\n\nBelow is a musical montage I've put together and I guess it shows why the animals walk funny...\n\nhttps://youtu.be/42XTAfMz3Ts\n\nIf you enjoyed reading this review please subscribe to my curator page. Thanks...\n\nhttp://store.steampowered.com/curator/6843548/",
